# --- dependencies (Vercel reinstalls these from the lockfiles) ---
node_modules
.venv
venv
__pycache__
*.pyc

# --- build output ---
.next
out
*.tsbuildinfo
# Next regenerates this on every build; it is in create-next-app's ignore list too.
next-env.d.ts

# --- deploy tooling ---
.vercel

# --- secrets ---
# This project needs no keys today (yfinance and Google News RSS are both
# keyless). If that ever changes, the value goes in Vercel's environment
# variables, never in the repo.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- editor / OS / agent local state ---
# PyCharm: workspace.xml holds absolute paths from this machine, and the rest is
# per-developer preference rather than project configuration.
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
# Claude Code's per-machine permission allowlist. A shared .claude/settings.json
# would be committable; the .local one never is.
.claude/settings.local.json

# --- test / lint artefacts ---
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- logs ---
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# --- the market scanner's private output ---
# Both are outputs of `scripts/scan_market.py` and both are deliberately
# untracked. `reports/` holds one buy/sell ranking per run — the most personal
# thing this repository can produce and the one file in it that is about the
# owner rather than about a company, which is the same argument that keeps the
# thesis journal in the browser. `.scan_cache/` is a per-day copy of provider
# data, regenerable and large.
.scan_cache/
reports/
